{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-8231" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $z=3-4\\text{i}$, calculate $z+\\overset{―}{z}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-8231" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we add a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always twice the real part of the complex number.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=3-4\\text{i},$ the real part is $Re(z)=3,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =2\\text{Re}(z) \\\\  & =2(3) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of adding the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=3-4\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=3+4\\text{i}.$\n\nAdding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =(3-4\\text{i})+(3+4\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(3+3)+\\text{i}(-4+4) \\\\  & =6+\\text{i}0 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-8231" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "616662c80c610779b81a0b5d99bfd523709843dfbc54727afca32a59845d0aa3"} {"question" "q-8231" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-8231" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "6-8\\text{i}"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-8231" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-16423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $z=4+9\\text{i}$, calculate $z\\overset{―}{z}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-16423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=4+9\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=4,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=9,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}+{9}^{2} \\\\  & =16+81 \\\\  & =97.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=4+9\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=4-9\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(4+9\\text{i})(4-9\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={4}^{2}+(4)(-9)\\text{i}+(4)(9)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(9)^{2} \\\\  & =16-36\\text{i}+36\\text{i}-(-1)(81) \\\\  & =16+81 \\\\  & =97.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-16423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "616662c80c610779b81a0b5d99bfd523709843dfbc54727afca32a59845d0aa3"} {"question" "q-16423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-16423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "65"] ["math" "85"] ["math" "85\\text{i}"] ["math" "97"] ["math" "97\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-16423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "97"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-72284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $z=-1-7\\text{i}$, calculate $z\\overset{―}{z}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-72284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=-1-7\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=-1,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=-7,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}+(-7)^{2} \\\\  & =1+49 \\\\  & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=-1-7\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=-1+7\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(-1-7\\text{i})(-1+7\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}+(-1)(7)\\text{i}+(-7)(-1)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(7)^{2} \\\\  & =1-7\\text{i}+7\\text{i}-(-1)(49) \\\\  & =1+49 \\\\  & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-72284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "616662c80c610779b81a0b5d99bfd523709843dfbc54727afca32a59845d0aa3"} {"question" "q-72284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-72284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "48"] ["math" "50"] ["math" "7\\text{i}"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "8\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-72284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "50"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-159757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $z=-9-\\text{i}$, calculate $z+\\overset{―}{z}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-159757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we add a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always twice the real part of the complex number.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=-9-\\text{i},$ the real part is $Re(z)=-9,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =2\\text{Re}(z) \\\\  & =2(-9) \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of adding the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=-9-\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=-9+\\text{i}.$\n\nAdding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =(-9-\\text{i})+(-9+\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(-9+(-9))+\\text{i}(-1+1) \\\\  & =-18+\\text{i}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-159757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "616662c80c610779b81a0b5d99bfd523709843dfbc54727afca32a59845d0aa3"} {"question" "q-159757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-159757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-18"] ["math" "-18\\text{i}"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "-8\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-159757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-18"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-279477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $z=-2-11\\text{i}$, then $z\\overset{―}{z}=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-279477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=-2-11\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=-2,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=-11,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & =(-2)^{2}+(-11)^{2} \\\\  & =4+121 \\\\  & =125.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=-2-11\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=-2+11\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(-2-11\\text{i})(-2+11\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(2)^{2}+(-2)(11)\\text{i}+(-11)(-2)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(11)^{2} \\\\  & =4-\\cancel{22\\text{i}}+\\cancel{22\\text{i}}-(-1)(121) \\\\  & =25+100 \\\\  & =125.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-279477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "616662c80c610779b81a0b5d99bfd523709843dfbc54727afca32a59845d0aa3"} {"question" "q-279477" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973745/state.json" "file_sha256" "492cc6becc5441b94ba30ada9525e7625a8de111c6275ed6785b325a8cd897d0"} {"question" "q-279477" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "125"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Acad